event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":102,"item_id":"rs_09a30bda3d6212a9016acb038f12188193b2405613aaf4159c","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering server-rendered forms**\n\nI'm thinking about implementing server-rendered forms with standard native navigation to ensure accessibility. When it comes to POST requests, I need to create a redirect and make sure to handle errors by rendering a 400 alert. The IDs will be auto-incrementing integers. Also, I'm considering using Node's built-in tests with child processes temporarily. It seems like we might not need JavaScript in the browser at all; plain HTML could suffice in this case. It’s interesting to weigh my options here!"}

event: response.reasoning_summary_part.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","sequence_number":103,"item_id":"rs_09a30bda3d6212a9016acb038f12188193b2405613aaf4159c","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Considering server-rendered forms**\n\nI'm thinking about implementing server-rendered forms with standard native navigation to ensure accessibility. When it comes to POST requests, I need to create a redirect and make sure to handle errors by rendering a 400 alert. The IDs will be auto-incrementing integers. Also, I'm considering using Node's built-in tests with child processes temporarily. It seems like we might not need JavaScript in the browser at all; plain HTML could suffice in this case. It’s interesting to weigh my options here!"}}

